turday of every month for a chance to see old friends and meet new people.&nbsp;</p><p>It might be especially nice for newcomers who have not had many chances to meet other villagers yet.&nbsp;</p><p>So, please come and do spread the word!&nbsp;</p><p>As parking is limited, please come on foot if at all possible.</p>','','full_html');
INSERT INTO `node__body` VALUES ('event','0','2064','2160','en','0','<p>The first Saturday of the month means that it’s time to pop into the village hall for the popular Repair Café with skilled sewers, electrical bods, general repairers and computer advice.&nbsp;</p><p>Successful repairs have included:&nbsp;kettles, jumpers, table lamps,&nbsp;garden tools, kitchen knives, wonky tables, picture frames, sports bags and more.&nbsp;</p><p>As well as repairs, many IT queries have been sorted: helping people keep their technology working better and for longer, or giving advice on the best courses of action.&nbsp;</p><p>If you have something that you would like advice on, or something that you’re not sure if it could be repaired, bring it along and the team of repairers will see what can be done.</p><p>With all the usual hot drinks, delicious cakes and warm welcome from the monthly coffee morning team.</p>','','full_html'),('event','0','2065','2161','en','0','<p>The next in the series of coffee mornings will be held in the Village Hall from 10.30am to 12.30.&nbsp;</p><p>Everybody is guaranteed a warm welcome!&nbsp;</p><p>Hot drinks, biscuits and cake will be provided for a small contribution to cover costs (suggested donations: £1 for a drink and £1- £1.50 for a piece of cake).&nbsp;</p><p>If you’d like to bake biscuits or a cake, please let Daniela Jones know (<a href="mailto:daniela.lynchets@gmail.com">daniela.lynchets@gmail.com</a>) and you can easily be reimbursed for the ingredients.</p><p>These coffee mornings are being held on the first Saturday of every month for a chance to see old friends and meet new people.&nbsp;</p><p>It might be especially nice for newcomers who have not had many chances to meet other villagers yet.&nbsp;</p><p>So, please come and do spread the word!&nbsp;</p><p>As parking is limited, please come on foot if at all possible.</p>','','full_html'),('event','0','2066','2162','en','0','<p>The first Saturday of the month means that it’s time to pop into the village hall for the popular Repair Café with skilled sewers, electrical bods, general repairers and computer advice.&nbsp;</p><p>Successful repairs have included:&nbsp;kettles, jumpers, table lamps,&nbsp;garden tools, kitchen knives, wonky tables, picture frames, sports bags and more.&nbsp;</p><p>As well as repairs, many IT queries have been sorted: helping people keep their technology working better and for longer, or giving advice on the best courses of action.&nbsp;</p><p>If you have something that you would like advice on, or something that you’re not sure if it could be repaired, bring it along and the team of repairers will see what can be done.</p><p>With all the usual hot drinks, delicious cakes and warm welcome from the monthly coffee morning team.</p>','','full_html');
