al&quot;,sans-serif">There will be a film each month, on Friday nights, in the run up to Christmas - starting at 7.30 (doors open from 7pm) in Buriton Village Hall</span></b></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_subtitle` VALUES ('event','0','1516','1578','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An inspiring true story</span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('event','0','1517','1579','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An endearing journey through space and time. </span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1518','1580','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The Buriton Ducklings Childcare Service features in a double-page spread in the Petersfield Post </span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1519','1581','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Childcare group makes poo bag dispensers</span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('event','0','1520','1582','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Everyone is welcome at this great Buriton tradition.</span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1521','1583','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Southern Water warn everyone about what is being flushed down local toilets and sinks.</span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1522','1584','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Buriton’s small Charity has big impact in rural Africa</span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_subtitle` VALUES ('news','0','1523','1585','en','0','<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">South Downs National Park highlights achievements in the village</span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('quickevent','0','1526','1588','en','0','<p><b data-uw-styling-context="true">Buriton Parish Council normally meets every alternate month throughout the year with meetings taking place in the Upper Hall, Buriton Village Hall, starting at 7pm with an opportunity for members of the public to ask questions or make comments in the Public Forum at 7.45pm. Due&nbsp;to&nbsp; Government Restrictions on Public Meetings during the Coronavirus Outbreak, Buriton Parish Council adopted alternative ways of working in order to continue with business whilst upholding democratic principles and compliance with the public health guidance. It&nbsp;is&nbsp;anticipated that this meeting of the Parish Council will take place in the main part of the&nbsp;village hall. Members of the public will be&nbsp;able to attend meetings, observe business and ask questions in a Public Forum session. If you have any queries about any Parish Council matter, please continue to contact our Clerk, Mrs Petra Norris, in the normal way: via 07943 536065 or&nbsp;<a data-uw-styling-context="true" href="mailto:buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk">buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;More details about the Parish Council can be found elsewhere on this website:&nbsp;<a data-uw-styling-context="true" href="http://www.buriton.info/parish-council">http://www.buriton.info/parish-council</a></b></p>\r\n','full_html'),('quickevent','0','1527','1589','en','0','<p><b data-uw-styling-context="true">Buriton Parish Council normally meets every alternate month throughout the year with meetings taking place in the Upper Hall, Buriton Village Hall, starting at 7pm with an opportunity for members of the public to ask questions or make comments in the Public Forum at 7.45pm. Due&nbsp;to Government Restrictions on Public Meetings during the Coronavirus Outbreak, Buriton Parish Council adopted alternative ways of working in order to continue with business whilst upholding democratic principles and compliance with the public health guidance. It&nbsp;is&nbsp;anticipated that this meeting of the Parish Council will take place in the main part of the&nbsp;village hall. Members of the public will be&nbsp;able to attend meetings, observe business and ask questions in a Public Forum session. If you have any queries about any Parish Council matter, please continue to contact our Clerk, Mrs Petra Norris, in the normal way: via 07943 536065 or&nbsp;<a data-uw-styling-context="true" href="mailto:buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk">buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;More details about the Parish Council can be found elsewhere on this website:&nbsp;<a data-uw-styling-context="true" href="http://www.buriton.info/parish-council">http://www.buriton.info/parish-council</a></b></p>\r\n','full_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_subtitle` VALUES ('quickevent','0','1528','1590','en','0','<p><strong>Buriton Parish Council normally meets every alternate month throughout the year with meetings taking place in the Upper Hall, Buriton Village Hall. In May the Council holds an Annual Meeting (commencing at 6.30pm) followed by its normal bi-monthly meeting (commencing at 7.15pm). There is an opportunity for members of the public to ask questions or make comments in either meeting with the Public Forum in the normal meeting scheduled for 8pm. Due&nbsp;to Government Restrictions on Public Meetings during the Coronavirus outbreak, Buriton Parish Council adopted alternative ways of working in order to continue with business whilst upholding democratic principles and compliance with the public health guidance. If you have any queries about any Parish Council matter, please continue to contact our Clerk, Mrs Petra Norris, in the normal way: via 07943 536065 or&nbsp;<a href="mailto:buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk">buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;More details about the Parish Council can be found elsewhere on this website:&nbsp;<a href="http://www.buriton.info/parish-council">http://www.buriton.info/parish-council</a></strong></p>\r\n','full_html'),('quickevent','0','1529','1591','en','0','<p><strong>Buriton Parish Council normally meets every alternate month throughout the year with meetings taking place in the Upper Hall, Buriton Village Hall, starting at 7pm with an opportunity for members of the public to ask questions or make comments in the Public Forum at 7.45pm. Due&nbsp;to Government Restrictions on Public Meetings during the Coronavirus Outbreak, Buriton Parish Council adopted alternative ways of working in order to continue with business whilst upholding democratic principles and compliance with the public health guidance. If necessary, meetings may be moved to take place in the main part of the&nbsp;village hall. Members of the public will be&nbsp;able to attend meetings, observe business and ask questions in a Public Forum session. If you have any queries about any Parish Council matter, please continue to contact our Clerk, Mrs Petra Norris, in the normal way: via 07943 536065 or&nbsp;<a href="mailto:buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk">buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;More details about the Parish Council can be found elsewhere on this website:&nbsp;<a href="http://www.buriton.info/parish-council">http://www.buriton.info/parish-council</a></strong></p>\r\n','full_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_subtitle` VALUES ('quickevent','0','1530','1592','en','0','<p><strong>Buriton Parish Council normally meets every alternate month throughout the year with meetings taking place in the Upper Hall, Buriton Village Hall, starting at 7pm with an opportunity for members of the public to ask questions or make comments in the Public Forum at 7.45pm. Due&nbsp;to Government Restrictions on Public Meetings during the Coronavirus Outbreak, Buriton Parish Council adopted alternative ways of working in order to continue with business whilst upholding democratic principles and compliance with the public health guidance. If necessary, meetings may be moved to take place in the main part of the&nbsp;village hall. Members of the public will be&nbsp;able to attend meetings, observe business and ask questions in a Public Forum session. If you have any queries about any Parish Council matter, please continue to contact our Clerk, Mrs Petra Norris, in the normal way: via 07943 536065 or&nbsp;<a href="mailto:buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk">buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;More details about the Parish Council can be found elsewhere on this website:&nbsp;<a href="http://www.buriton.info/parish-council">http://www.buriton.info/parish-council</a></strong></p>\r\n','full_html'),('quickevent','0','1531','1593','en','0','<p><strong>Buriton Parish Council normally meets every alternate month throughout the year with meetings taking place in the Upper Hall, Buriton Village Hall, starting at 7pm with an opportunity for members of the public to ask questions or make comments in the Public Forum at 7.45pm. Due&nbsp;to&nbsp; Government Restrictions on Public Meetings during the Coronavirus Outbreak, Buriton Parish Council adopted alternative ways of working in order to continue with business whilst upholding democratic principles and compliance with the public health guidance. If necessary, meetings may be moved to take place in the main part of the&nbsp;village hall. Members of the public will be&nbsp;able to attend meetings, observe business and ask questions in a Public Forum session. If you have any queries about any Parish Council matter, please continue to contact our Clerk, Mrs Petra Norris, in the normal way: via 07943 536065 or&nbsp;<a href="mailto:buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk">buritonparishcouncil@hotmail.co.uk</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;More details about the Parish Council can be found elsewhere on this website:&nbsp;<a href="http://www.buriton.info/parish-council">http://www.buriton.info/parish-council</a></strong></p>\r\n','full_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_subtitle` VALUES ('news','0','1532','1594','en','0','<p>The County Council has produced a short video about the community''s pollinator initiative</p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1533','1595','en','0','<p><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="line-height:107%"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="line-height:107%">Ideas to help the community’s ‘Climate Change Challenge’</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1534','1596','en','0','<p><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="line-height:107%"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="line-height:107%">Exhibition at the Petersfield Museum from 24 November to 5 March</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('event','0','1535','1597','en','0','<p><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="line-height:105%"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="line-height:105%">Now to be held in the Manor Barn: 1pm to 4pm</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1540','1602','en','0','<p><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="line-height:107%"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Join the Buriton Climate Change Challenge</span></span></span></b></p>\r\n','full_html'),('event','0','1541','1603','en','0','<p><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background:white"><span style="line-height:normal"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="color:#333333">New trees for old!!</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n','full_html'),('event','0','1547','1609','en','0','<p><strong>Illustrated talk about fascinating history and natural history</strong></p>\r\n','full_html'),('news','0','1548','1610','en','0','<p><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background:white"><span style="font-fam